WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.150
Dr. Jack Bright is a man known by many names,
and whether that name is“Oh God No” or

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:11.290
just Jack, if you’ve spent any amount of
time here on SCP Explained, you’ve surely

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:14.060
at least heard of the good doctor one or twice.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:19.310
He’s a high-ranking senior staff member
at Site-19, one of the Foundation’s most

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:24.480
notable facilities, and has served as a director
and important member of the Foundation’s

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.359
upper ranks for decades.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:30.029
Of course, you wouldn’t be able to tell
that by looking at him, because depending

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:36.900
on the current circumstances, Dr. Bright might
not look a day over 13, or 80, or 90, or he

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.620
might just be a chimpanzee.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:44.650
This is because Dr. Bright, in his younger
days, came into contact with SCP-963, a metal

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.760
amulet that gives its wearer’s consciousness
immortality.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.760
When the amulet is moved from one body to
another, Dr. Bright’s consciousness moves

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:59.180
with it, allowing him to occupy a variety
of bodies, from animals to old ladies, Dr.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.570
Bright has been them all.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:05.320
Heck, Bright’s body-swapping abilities have
even proven themselves to be incredibly useful

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:10.130
for the Foundation, so the guy’s able to
get some actual work done when he’s not

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.400
goofing off.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.940
In undercover operations, Dr. Bright has been
used to infiltrate areas that the Foundation

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:20.380
would typically have trouble reaching, or
where clandestine operations are the best

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.380
course of action.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:27.590
In the 2000 United States Election, Dr. Bright
briefly occupied the body of George Bush in

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:33.290
order for the Foundation to investigate political
opponent Al Gore’s activities without suspicion.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.680
But that mess is a story for another day.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.470
Today, we’re going to be taking a look at
a different side of Dr. Jack Bright.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:46.790
One that isn’t so overt, one that’s lurking
behind the joking facade and silly antics

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:50.190
so commonly associated with Bright’s identity.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:55.870
This is SCP Explained, and we’d like to
welcome you into the complicated, dramatic,

00:01:55.870 --> 00:02:02.960
and ultimately tragic world of the Bright
family, specifically, the story of SCP-590.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.431
Your consciousness being immortal certainly
has its perks.

00:02:05.431 --> 00:02:08.000
For one, you can’t die!

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.030
On the other hand, you can’t die.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:15.090
We all know the old cliche about immortality,
how your friends and loved ones will grow

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:18.670
old and die off while you’ll stay the same
age.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.500
How centuries will start to feel like months.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.120
How your mind will eventually crumble under
the weight of countless years and experiences,

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:29.620
because no man was made to live this long.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:33.920
But while it’s a cliche for us, it’s reality
for Dr. Bright.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:40.020
He’s painfully aware of how futile his situation
is, and behind closed doors, it scares him.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:45.630
Dr. Bright struggles intensely with existential
depression, and for good reason too, right

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:50.830
now he might be fine, but in the relatively
near future, he’ll start experiencing that

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:56.640
cycle of death and rebirth of those around
him and himself, and over time, that cycle

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.730
will just keep repeating.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:04.860
Body after body, friend after friend, tragedy
after tragedy, in the long term, Dr. Bright

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.430
knows that his life cannot have a happy ending.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:13.420
It’s most likely because of this biting,
inevitable future that Bright makes the most

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:20.020
of his time with those around him in the Foundation,
making himself known as a charming, goofy

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.069
personality brimming with quirks and zaniness.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:27.959
The part of Bright that makes others laugh
does so because deep down, Bright needs something

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:30.250
to take his mind off of his situation.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:34.790
He wants the same type of familiarity and
comfort that he brings to other people.

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:39.580
But Bright’s public-facing persona is often
torn to shreds in private.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:45.160
On top of being an undying soul, Bright has
to contend with an even more stressful experience:

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.550
his family.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:50.890
The Bright family is a colorful assortment
of old blood that has run the inner circle

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.750
of the anomalous world for generations.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:57.480
There are members of the Bright family that
were there when the First Administrator signed

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:03.800
the policy that created the SCP Foundation,
members who served time on the Overseer Council,

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.510
and even those who operate outside of the
parameters of the Foundation.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:14.160
Dr. Bright is just one among many other individuals
of major anomalous significance in his bloodline,

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.349
and it’s only fitting that every family
has its issues.

00:04:17.349 --> 00:04:22.620
For the Brights, all strong personalities
who hold positions of power in various places

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:27.319
across the anomalous world, unity isn’t
exactly a strong point.

00:04:27.319 --> 00:04:32.199
In fact, most of the family isn’t anywhere
near each other, each member existing in their

00:04:32.199 --> 00:04:37.639
own bubble, working towards their own individual
goals that often do not align with the rest

00:04:37.639 --> 00:04:38.909
of their kin.

00:04:38.909 --> 00:04:43.229
But there are occasions when the Bright Family
all come together to sneer at one another

00:04:43.229 --> 00:04:48.729
from across a table and enjoy a nice, loving
reunion, though these meetings are often called

00:04:48.729 --> 00:04:52.030
out of necessity, and are far and few between.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:56.139
This gathering of anomalous individuals is
deemed important enough by the Foundation

00:04:56.139 --> 00:05:00.259
to have its own designated security term,
nicknamed “Code Brown”.

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:06.129
When a Code Brown is issued, it can only mean
that the Brights are locked away in a room,

00:05:06.129 --> 00:05:11.259
convening, arguing, and scheming over something
of great importance to them, and the rest

00:05:11.259 --> 00:05:14.350
of the world should stay out of their family
business.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:18.569
And when Jack Bright got his latest call for
a family meeting from one of the family members

00:05:18.569 --> 00:05:24.069
he was on speaking terms with, he could only
think of just how bad of an idea that was.

00:05:24.069 --> 00:05:29.410
It had been quite some time since Bright saw
the rest of his family, and he didn’t particularly

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:31.949
look forward to when they would meet again.

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:36.779
In the time since then, Bright had been taking
care of TJ, his younger brother, whose story

00:05:36.779 --> 00:05:38.490
is nearly as tragic as Jacks.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:43.059
Don’t worry, we’ll get back to the events
of the family reunion soon enough.

00:05:43.059 --> 00:05:46.059
For now, let’s have a look at TJ Bright.

00:05:46.059 --> 00:05:51.180
TJ was a product of the cruel, brutal attitude
the early Foundation took out on the objects

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.839
it contained.

00:05:52.839 --> 00:05:57.900
Needlessly cold containment procedures that
denied basic needs for human anomalies, pointless

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:03.919
tests that often resulted in death or worse,
and a general lack of regard for decency or

00:06:03.919 --> 00:06:05.129
ethics.

00:06:05.129 --> 00:06:09.990
This archaic era would come to an end upon
the formation of the Ethics Committee, a board

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:14.649
formed in the upper ranks of the Foundation
that would enforce a better treatment of the

00:06:14.649 --> 00:06:20.409
objects contained by the organization, with
severe consequences for those that disobeyed

00:06:20.409 --> 00:06:23.059
the new, more humane doctrine.

00:06:23.059 --> 00:06:26.860
But in the case of TJ Bright, there was nothing
the Committee could do.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:33.309
TJ, who had been given the designation of
SCP-590 long ago, was an ordinary person who

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:38.059
happened to have anomalous abilities, like
countless others that the Foundation had dealt

00:06:38.059 --> 00:06:39.400
with before.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:44.830
He appeared to be permanently 16 years old,
never aging or changing in appearance once

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:47.050
during his time in containment.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:51.330
The abilities in question that had caught
the attention of the Foundation were TJ’s

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.659
inherent power to cure illness.

00:06:53.659 --> 00:06:59.729
Physical, mental, injuries, and wounds, TJ
could cure them all with just a touch of his

00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:00.729
hand.

00:07:00.729 --> 00:07:02.749
But at an unfortunate cost.

00:07:02.749 --> 00:07:07.270
Whatever injury TJ would cure, it would be
mirrored onto his own body.

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:12.569
A giant, gaping wound could be healed by TJ,
but the aftereffects of such, such as scar

00:07:12.569 --> 00:07:18.050
tissue and any lasting side effects, would
later appear on his own body, leaving the

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:21.960
boy to feel the pain of everyone he touched
and healed.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:28.099
The early Foundation needlessly exploited
SCP-590’s abilities in tests and procedures,

00:07:28.099 --> 00:07:31.199
testing the limits of TJ’s body and its
abilities.

00:07:31.199 --> 00:07:35.419
This, of course, was carried out without the
knowledge of his brother, Dr. Bright, who

00:07:35.419 --> 00:07:40.529
at the time did not have enough pull or power
within the organization to save his brother.

00:07:40.529 --> 00:07:46.119
He could only watch and hope that one day
SCP-590 could live a better life outside of

00:07:46.119 --> 00:07:52.779
his cell, as TJ Bright, and not a number on
a placard to be experimented with so casually.

00:07:52.779 --> 00:07:58.199
The Foundation’s experiments with TJ sometimes
involved the use of SCP-500, an all-curing

00:07:58.199 --> 00:08:04.860
panacea that would fully heal SCP-590, and
bring him back to full health, a state that

00:08:04.860 --> 00:08:09.209
would later be reverted when the Foundation
started their experiments with the boy once

00:08:09.209 --> 00:08:10.209
again.

00:08:10.209 --> 00:08:15.020
TJ had endured immeasurable pain, and as a
result had suffered a broken, mental state

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.430
over the years.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:22.009
As time went by, and things within the Foundation
had started to change, including Jack Bright’s

00:08:22.009 --> 00:08:26.419
prominence, he worked as hard as he could
to push through bureaucratic red tape and

00:08:26.419 --> 00:08:30.749
work out a solution that would leave TJ in
a less torturous position.

00:08:30.749 --> 00:08:36.750
And when the time came, it was Jack Bright
who made the call to have SCP-590 cure a variety

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:42.320
of specific mental conditions that would leave
the boy in a dulled state, unable to fully

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:47.700
comprehend the pain he endures, should the
Foundation ever have to utilize TJ’s abilities

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.700
again.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:53.150
Bright’s decision to do this to his brother
was questionable, and a part of the doctor

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:58.600
regrets it to this day, but at the time, it
seemed like a more preferable option than

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:02.970
having SCP-590 be fully aware of what was
happening to him.

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:08.160
Unfortunately, the idea that TJ’s reduced
mental capacities would prevent him from understanding

00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:13.900
what was occuring to him was a misunderstanding,
and TJ was still more than capable of perceiving

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:17.680
what was happening to him, and that was pain.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:23.100
He knew he was being hurt, he knew he wasn’t
loved, and even though his mind was unlike

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:28.060
Brights or those who experimented with him,
he felt the same things they did.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:32.430
By the time of the reunion, TJ was fully in
the care of Dr. Bright.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:37.220
Eventually, the modern Foundation worked out
that it was doing the poor boy more harm than

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:42.430
good to keep him locked up in a cell all day,
and Bright, who was now one of the most notable

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:47.750
and important individuals in the Foundation,
was able to pull enough strings to get TJ

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:48.770
out of confinement.

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:55.410
Now, he could truly rest without worry that
he would be exploited and abused, safe alongside

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:57.120
his older brother.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:01.370
Inside the meeting room, all of the famous
figures of the Bright family, well, the ones

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.740
that were alive at least, were there.

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:08.930
Dr. Bright sat alongside TJ, who occupied
himself with a coloring book and a set of

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:10.080
crayons.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:16.050
From across the table was Mikell Bright, better
known as Overseer O5-6, a former Foundation

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:19.580
agent who operated under the name of ‘Cowboy’.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:26.050
O5-6 was a hardened individual, with a heavy
interest in firearms and a whole lot of luck

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.460
on his side.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:32.280
Mikell and Jack, almost at the same time,
both fired out remarks about how bad of an

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:34.820
idea they felt this reunion was.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:40.050
The one who called the reunion was their elder
sister, Claire Bright, whose aged body felt

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:45.300
notably out of place among the collection
of forever-young Brights, whether it was Jack’s

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:51.960
body-hopping, TJ’s longevity, or Mikell’s
use of SCP-006, the Overseer Council’s “Fountain

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.960
of Youth”, to keep himself young for an
extended period of time.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.920
Also present was Yoric Elroy, Jack Bright’s
grandson, and a man who always happened to

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.110
be at the right place at the right time, even
if he himself felt that it was wrong.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:04.340
As the three of them discussed the state of
Claire Bright’s apparent aging situation,

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:08.070
Yoric remarked that he thought she was involved
with that incident at Site-23.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:13.990
This, Dr. Bright knew, was referring to an
incident he’d rather forget, where a reality

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:19.170
bender contained by the Foundation attempted
to give the Bright family, himself, Mikell,

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:24.680
and TJ included, a happy ending, where they
would be cured of their ailments and allowed

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:26.850
to live ordinary lives.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:31.310
Of course, this was just the product of a
reality bend, and the fantasy quickly fell

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:34.180
apart when the Brights realized what was going
on.

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:37.880
Jack rathered not dwell on what could have
been.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:42.360
Across from Yoric was Foundation Agent Serra
Argent, one of the younger members of the

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:47.200
Bright family, who worked as the Overseer
Council’s Hand Sinister, a special title

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:51.780
granted to an assassin used by the Council
to sort out messy business for them.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:56.380
The previous Hand Sinister was none other
than Mikell Bright, whose pearl revolvers

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:59.510
that came with the position now belonged to
Serra.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:03.450
Mikell was growing impatient and asked how
long it would take for the rest of the family

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.450
to show up.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:08.320
The rest of the family being the Brights that
weren’t involved in the Foundation.

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:13.210
The powerful individuals who had worked their
way into various groups of interests and aspects

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.870
of the anomalous world.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:20.120
While some directly opposed the Foundation
and its mission and others were neutral, they

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:23.470
were all Brights, which meant that their presence
was necessary.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:28.770
While the two sides sometimes worked together,
there was always an air of bad blood and poor

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:30.300
trust between them.

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:34.430
Dr. Bright in particular was not looking forward
to the rest of this meeting.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:39.210
The first to arrive was an individual named
Nobody, who the Foundation had a difficult

00:12:39.210 --> 00:12:40.870
time keeping up with.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:45.730
Nobody was a title granted from one person
to the next, who each worked towards a greater

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:51.600
plan that only Nobody knew the specific details
of, leaving the Foundation completely unaware

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.290
of the group’s larger interests.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:58.760
Nobody’s voice was impossible to source,
and her appearance was even harder to pin

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:00.860
down, but she was there.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:04.840
Nobody circled around the table, remarking
that the other side of the family had sent

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:09.580
her first to make sure that the Foundation
Brights were all abiding by the rules.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:15.360
At one point in time, Nobody did have another
name, but in becoming the next Nobody, she

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.650
left her previous life all behind.

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:22.610
The next to arrive was Claire Lumineux the
Second, a human with electromagnetic abilities

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.790
whose motives were largely unknown.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:29.800
When she pulled back the chair to sit down,
sparks flew in the air, briefly startling

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:31.490
the rest of the room.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:36.750
After that came David Blindman, a gruff, sunglasses-wearing
member of the Serpent’s Hand, a group of

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:41.490
anomalous individuals who work to free anomalies
from the confinements of the Foundation, who

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:43.460
they call jailers.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:49.040
Blindman was Mikell’s son, and possessed
the anomalous ability to see into the future.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:54.470
He was the unofficial representative of the
Unnumbered Brood, a subsection of the Bright

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:58.960
family consisting of Mikell's illegitimate
children from his wilder days as a free-roaming

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:04.070
Foundation Agent, and a constant reminder
to the overseer of his past.

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:08.779
Naturally, Mikell was less than pleased to
see his son arrive.

00:14:08.779 --> 00:14:14.110
And then there was Evelyn Navon, who levitated
into the room wearing a traditional hijab

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:15.110
and dress.

00:14:15.110 --> 00:14:20.180
Evelyn was one of the original 13 founding
members of the SCP Foundation, and the matriarch

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:22.270
of most of the Bright family.

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:26.779
Unfortunately, Evelyn was kicked off of the
Council for reasons unknown, but rumor has

00:14:26.779 --> 00:14:31.900
it that it had something to do with her terrible
experiments as a genius geneticist, creating

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:36.170
monsters by splicing the DNA of the ordinary
and the anomalous.

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:41.890
She’s sold her work to groups of interest
such as Dr. Wondertainment or Prometheus Labs,

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:45.600
who benefited from having such fine test subjects
to work with.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:50.330
Her current activities are largely unknown,
but as the rest of the family knew, they couldn’t

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:51.720
be anything good.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:56.840
The final member of the Bright Family to enter
was the only one who was trusted by all of

00:14:56.840 --> 00:15:03.360
them, and that was a man of many names, who
was most commonly referred to as Tamlin.

00:15:03.360 --> 00:15:08.660
Tamlin was a mysterious individual who existed
for centuries, far longer than any other member

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:09.870
of the family.

00:15:09.870 --> 00:15:15.440
He had something to do with time, but no one
was quite sure what it was that he did, but

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:20.070
they all knew that he was important, and that
he was the only one who attempted to keep

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:23.970
peace and balance between the various factions
of the family.

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:29.400
Tamlin took a mental count of the room, realized
everyone was present, and addressed them all,

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.470
ready to explain why they were there.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:36.210
Collectively, the family came to realize that
the one who called the meeting, Claire Bright,

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:37.440
was not there.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:42.430
Tamlin solemnly explained that she had passed
away, and he had called the family together

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:47.260
in her stead to present a video tape containing
her dying wish.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:51.650
The tape was concocted through Claire and
Tamlin’s time shenanigans, and featured

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:56.920
a recording of Claire who, through Tamlin’s
abilities to travel through and control time,

00:15:56.920 --> 00:16:01.570
was able to respond and interact with the
members of the family in the room.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:06.330
As morbid as Dr. Bright felt this was, he
would make sure to treasure this final interaction

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.490
with his sister.

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:12.120
Claire’s recording contained her will, and
with Tamlin’s help, she distributed gifts

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:16.710
to the other members of the family, final
remembrances she had collected from across

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:19.050
the anomalous world for them to cherish.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:22.330
An egg with a universe inside of it for Evelyn.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:25.800
The literal sword of Damocles to hang over
Mikell’s head.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:30.850
Jack Bright’s first-ever bottle of whiskey
that he made so many years before.

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:33.540
Documents she entrusted to her daughter, Claire
II.

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:39.160
When it came time for TJ’s gift, however,
the boy suddenly grew serious and declined

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.160
it.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:44.270
The recording of Claire understood, and stated
that if he didn’t want it, then she would

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:47.510
instead have Tamlin give it to someone who
needed it.

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:51.850
Dr. Bright could only wonder what it was that
she had planned to give TJ, but it seemed

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:57.140
like the boy’s selfless nature had won again,
and he was unable to accept it.

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:59.840
After the gifts had been distributed, the
tape cut out.

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:04.170
Tamlin stated that this was all that Claire
had recorded, and that she wanted her death

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:09.179
to bring the family together once again, to
remind them that they were family.

00:17:09.179 --> 00:17:13.860
Claire’s sincerity had brought the room
to silence, each member of the family engaged

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.149
in deep thought.

00:17:15.149 --> 00:17:19.289
As Tamlin gave parting remarks, one by one,
each member left.

00:17:19.289 --> 00:17:24.639
Mikell was embarrassed by the ordeal, immediately
trying to revert back to his Overseer mindset,

00:17:24.639 --> 00:17:25.639
but he couldn’t.

00:17:25.639 --> 00:17:27.589
Claire’s loss was already affecting him.

00:17:27.589 --> 00:17:33.090
In the end, there was only Tamlin, who left
a single blue rose on top of the VCR player

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:39.059
that contained Claire’s recording in remembrance
of someone he felt almost understood him.

00:17:39.059 --> 00:17:44.309
As Dr. Bright left the meeting, he still felt
conflicted about his family, but at the very

00:17:44.309 --> 00:17:47.820
least, he felt there was progress being made.

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:52.330
After all, they had all been in the same room
for more than 10 minutes without trying to

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:53.669
kill one another.

00:17:53.669 --> 00:17:58.320
He glanced at the boy at his side, wondering
if he made the right decision all those years

00:17:58.320 --> 00:17:59.320
ago.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:03.429
While that much, and most of his job with
the Foundation was uncertain, he knew one

00:18:03.429 --> 00:18:06.980
thing for a fact: he had to protect TJ.

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:12.780
Now go check out “SCP Immortal Dr. Bright
Explained” and “SCP-963 What Would You

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:18.020
Do If You Were Immortal Like Dr. Jack Bright?”
for more of the wacky world of Jack Bright!

